# CompTIA A+ — Cables & Connectors

What is the maximum speed of USB 2.0?
---
480 Mbps
~ 12 Mbps
~ 5 Gbps
~ 480 Gbps
---
Hi-Speed. USB 1.1 tops out at 12 Mbps, USB 3.0 at 5 Gbps.

What is the maximum speed of USB 3.0 (USB 3.1 Gen 1)?
---
5 Gbps
~ 480 Mbps
~ 10 Gbps
~ 20 Gbps
---
SuperSpeed, usually a blue port. Gen 2 doubles it to 10 Gbps.

Which connector does a wired Ethernet LAN cable use?
---
RJ45
~ RJ11
~ F-type
~ BNC
---
Eight pins. RJ11 is the smaller six-position phone jack used by DSL.

Which cable standard is rated for 10 Gbps at a full 100 metres?
---
Cat 6a
~ Cat 5e
~ Cat 6
~ Cat 3
---
Plain Cat 6 manages 10 Gbps only to about 55 metres. Cat 5e is rated for 1 Gbps.

Which connector does coaxial cable for cable internet use?
---
F-type
~ RJ45
~ BNC
~ SC
---
The screw-on connector on RG-6 coax from the cable company.

Which cable type is immune to electromagnetic interference?
---
Fiber optic
~ Shielded twisted pair
~ Coaxial
~ Cat 6a
---
It carries light, not electricity. It also spans kilometres where copper is limited to 100 metres.

What is the maximum SATA III transfer rate?
---
6 Gbps
~ 3 Gbps
~ 1.5 Gbps
~ 16 Gbps
---
About 600 MB/s in practice, which is why fast SSDs moved to NVMe over PCIe.

Which video connector carries analog signal only?
---
VGA
~ HDMI
~ DisplayPort
~ DVI-D
---
The blue 15-pin D-sub. DVI-D and HDMI are digital only, DVI-I carries both.

Which connector do both Thunderbolt 3 and 4 use?
---
USB-C
~ Mini DisplayPort
~ USB-A
~ Lightning
---
Thunderbolt 1 and 2 used Mini DisplayPort. Look for the lightning-bolt icon to tell a plain USB-C port apart.

Which video interface commonly carries audio along with video?
---
HDMI
~ VGA
~ DVI-D
~ Composite
---
DisplayPort does too. VGA and DVI carry video only.

Which power connector does a modern 3.5-inch hard drive use?
---
SATA 15-pin
~ Molex 4-pin
~ Berg 4-pin
~ PCIe 6-pin
---
The flat 15-pin plug from the PSU. Molex survives mainly on fans and old drives.

What does a punchdown tool do?
---
Seats wires into a keystone jack or patch panel
~ Crimps RJ45 plugs onto cable
~ Tests continuity of each pair
~ Traces a cable inside a wall
---
The crimper handles plugs. A toner probe traces the cable. A cable tester checks the pairs.
